{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775326555-gJ3LvIeNnxCr9kvJE7Aj","role":"assistant","created":1775326563,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The exchange rate information doesn't seem to be in the Treasury Bulletin files. I'll need to use standard historical exchange rates for USD/INR. Let me search online or use known historical data.\n\nActually, for historical USD/INR exchange rates:\n- 1964: The Indian rupee was pegged to the USD at a fixed rate. The pegged rate was 4.7619 INR per USD (this was before the 1966 devaluation)\n- But I need to find the annual average USD/INR exchange rate\n\nLet me think about the history:\n- The rupee was pegged to the pound sterling initially, and the USD was pegged to gold\n- In 1947, the rupee was valued at 3.30 rupees per dollar\n- In 1966, the rupee was devalued from 4.7619 to 7.5 rupees per dollar\n\nActually, let me verify this. For the period 1964-1966, India maintained a fixed exchange rate of 4.7619 rupees per US dollar (since the devaluation of 1949). However, there was also a \"free\" market rate in addition to the official rate.\n\nWait, but the question specifically asks for \"annual average USD/INR exchange rate for the corresponding years\". Let me search for this more specifically.\n\nActually, I need to be careful. The question asks for conversion using \"annual average USD/INR exchange rate for the corresponding years\". This suggests that there should be actual annual average exchange rates available, not just the fixed official rate.\n\nLet me look for more specific historical data. Actually, during this period (1964-1966), India did have a pegged exchange rate. But the question seems to expect that I'll use some annual average rates.\n\nLooking at historical data more carefully:\n- Prior to June 1966: 4.7619 INR per USD (official rate)\n- After June 1966: 7.5 INR per USD\n\n\n- I'm uncertain about the annual average for 1964-1965, as the official rate was fixed at 4.7619\n\nI'm exploring alternati